1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Aminoff_nr_456#TAB_114 '''Bernt Gustaf Aminoff'''], född 1785-05-30 på [https://bebyggelsenamn.sls.fi/bebyggelsenamn/1221/hindrabole-raseborg/ Hindraböle] i Pojo socken. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rustmästare''' vid Nylands infanteriregemente 1800. Kadett vid Haapaniemi 1802. Kornett vid Nylands dragonregemente 1805. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Transporterad''' till norra skånska infantanteriegementet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gick i westfalisk''' tjänst. Blev där löjtnant och slutligen major. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stupade vid''' Smolensk 1812.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Grok''' seemed to know about the Westphalians...
2 CONT
2 CONT During Napoleon's 1812 invasion of Russia, Major Aminoff, a Finnish-origin officer serving in the Westphalian VIII Corps (under Junot), was killed on 19 August 1812 at the Battle of Valutino (also known as Valutino Gora or Lubino)
2 CONC . This engagement occurred about 20–25 km east of Smolensk, near the villages of Valutino and Lubino (coordinates approx. 54°49′23″N 32°14′28″E), as part of the broader Smolensk operations. The Westphalians participated in failed 
2 CONC attempts to cut off the Russian retreat, suffering heavy losses in the fighting. While the main Battle of Smolensk took place on 16-18 August, Aminoff fell in the key follow-up action on the 19th.
